From: Joseph Marrero Corchado <jmarrero@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:27:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] initramfs: Enforce fs-verity for strict composefs boots

A strict composefs command line must not inherit an insecure repository
policy from meta.json. Verify the opened image against the requested
digest and mount that same file descriptor with verity required. This
preserves valid boots from older installations with unprotected metadata
and also verifies images resolved through named refs.

Add unit and TMT coverage for stripped image verity, metadata replacement,
wrong image refs, tampered data objects, and explicitly relaxed mounts.
The mount suite passes with the fix and rejects the original behavior.

